1. ARTIFACT ENGINE DESIGN PRINCIPLE
The OneDraft Artifact & Storage Management Engine provides the persistent storage boundary for every generated, uploaded, imported, rendered, exported, and finalized project artifact.
The system shall distinguish between:
Project state
The computational architectural model stored by OneDraft.
Artifact metadata
The database record describing a stored artifact.
Artifact content
The actual binary or textual object stored in object storage.
Artifact version
A specific immutable content state.
Artifact derivative
A generated representation derived from another artifact.
Artifact package
A controlled collection of artifacts representing a project deliverable.
Artifact provenance
The complete chain identifying how an artifact was created.
The artifact engine therefore becomes the persistent bridge between the computational project model and physical deliverables.

2. STORAGE ARCHITECTURE
The storage architecture shall initially consist of:
OneDraft Application
        ↓
Artifact Service
        ↓
PostgreSQL Metadata
        ↓
Object Storage
        ↓
Artifact Content
PostgreSQL stores metadata, relationships, hashes, ownership, version information and provenance.
Object storage stores the actual artifact payload.
The application shall never treat an object-storage path alone as the authoritative identity of an artifact.

3. STORAGE SCHEMAS
The PostgreSQL database shall initially use:
storage
artifacts
artifact_versions
artifact_derivatives
artifact_links
artifact_packages
artifact_package_items
uploads
downloads
provenance
The existing OneDraft logical schemas remain authoritative for project, model, documentation, compliance, validation, revision and audit data.

4. UNIVERSAL ARTIFACT RULES
All artifact identifiers use:
UUID
All timestamps use:
TIMESTAMPTZ
All timestamps are stored in UTC.
Artifacts are immutable after publication.
A new content state creates a new artifact version rather than overwriting an existing version.
Normal application operation must never silently replace historical artifact content.

