8. CONTENT HASH
Every immutable artifact version shall receive a cryptographic content hash.
The initial implementation shall support:
SHA-256
The hash is calculated from the stored content.
Conceptually:
CONTENT
 ↓
SHA-256
 ↓
CONTENT_HASH
 ↓
ARTIFACT_VERSION
The content hash provides deterministic identity verification.

9. STORAGE OBJECT KEY
Object storage keys shall not expose uncontrolled user-provided filenames as authoritative storage paths.
The initial object-key structure shall be conceptually:
projects/{project_id}/artifacts/{artifact_id}/versions/{version_id}/content
Optional derivatives:
projects/{project_id}/artifacts/{artifact_id}/versions/{version_id}/derivatives/{derivative_id}/content
This prevents filename collisions and preserves deterministic storage organization.

10. OBJECT STORAGE ABSTRACTION
The application shall communicate with object storage through a storage abstraction.
Conceptually:
StorageProvider
