30. IMMUTABILITY RULE
Once an artifact version becomes:
FINAL
or:
ACCEPTED
its content must never be modified in place.
Any change produces:
NEW ARTIFACT VERSION
and, where appropriate:
NEW REVISION

31. ARTIFACT STATUS
Initial statuses:
PENDING
ACTIVE
SUPERSEDED
ARCHIVED
DELETED
FINAL
ACCEPTED
A DELETED artifact retains its metadata where required for provenance and audit.
The physical object may be subject to lifecycle-management policy rather than immediate deletion.

32. RETENTION POLICY
Retention shall be configurable by artifact class.
Initial classes:
TEMPORARY
PROJECT
HISTORICAL
