worker scratch files
temporary exports
preview images
transient conversion files
These may be automatically removed after a configured retention period.
Temporary artifacts must never be used as the authoritative source for a finalized deliverable.

34. ARTIFACT CLEANUP
Cleanup operations shall be asynchronous.
Conceptually:
IDENTIFY EXPIRED ARTIFACT
 ↓
VERIFY NOT REFERENCED
 ↓
VERIFY NOT FINAL
 ↓
VERIFY RETENTION POLICY
 ↓
DELETE OBJECT
 ↓
RECORD CLEANUP EVENT
The cleanup worker must never delete an artifact solely because it appears unused in one table.

35. STORAGE INTEGRITY CHECK
The system shall periodically verify stored artifacts.
Conceptually:
ARTIFACT VERSION
 ↓
READ OBJECT
 ↓
HASH CONTENT
 ↓
COMPARE STORED HASH
If the hashes differ:
INTEGRITY_FAILURE
The system shall preserve the metadata and create an audit event.

