58. STORAGE TRANSACTION BOUNDARY
Artifact metadata and object content are separate systems.
Therefore:
DATABASE TRANSACTION
and:
OBJECT STORAGE OPERATION
cannot always participate in one native transaction.
The system shall therefore use explicit artifact lifecycle states.
Example:
PENDING
 ↓
OBJECT_UPLOADED
 ↓
VERIFIED
 ↓
COMMITTED
If database finalization fails, reconciliation can safely identify the orphaned object.

59. STORAGE RECONCILIATION
A periodic reconciliation worker shall compare:
DATABASE ARTIFACT RECORDS
against:
OBJECT STORAGE OBJECTS
It shall identify:
missing objects
orphaned objects
hash mismatches
unexpected objects
incomplete uploads
No automatic destructive correction shall occur without lifecycle-policy verification.

60. ORPHAN MANAGEMENT
An object is considered potentially orphaned when:
object exists
AND
no committed artifact version references it
The system shall initially mark it:
ORPHAN_CANDIDATE
before any deletion occurs.

